&lt;p&gt;As we continue to grow, we are seeking a talented Software Engineer to join our Risk Management team and help build first-party risk management features that help our customers identify, assess, and mitigate organizational risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a full-stack engineer with 3–5 years of experience who cares about building software that is correct, reliable, and genuinely useful. You thrive working across the stack — comfortable designing APIs in the morning and refining React components in the afternoon. You take pride in writing code that is well-tested and maintainable, and you understand that in a compliance domain, data integrity is not optional.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are excited by the challenge of translating complex domain logic — risk scoring, control testing, framework alignment — into clean, intuitive product experiences. You are comfortable asking questions, engaging in design discussions, and owning features end-to-end. You work well in a collaborative, async-first environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer on the Risk Management team, your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and ship first-party risk management features including risk register, inherent and residual risk scoring, and risk lifecycle workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and extend control testing and monitoring capabilities — automated evidence checks, test cadence scheduling, and pass/fail logic tied to compliance outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrations with compliance frameworks including SOC 2, ISO 27001, NIST CSF, and others — enabling customers to map their controls and risks to the standards that matter to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and designers to translate compliance domain requirements into reliable, intuitive product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write backend services and APIs in C# (.NET), Node.js, and/or Python that are performant, well-documented, and testable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain React/TypeScript front-end components that surface complex risk data in clean, actionable dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews and code reviews, contributing to engineering quality across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with QA to ensure correctness — you understand that in a compliance product, data integrity issues have real consequences for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of software engineering experience in a product-focused company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript for front-end development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least one of Java Springboot, Node.js, or Python for back-end API development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across the full stack — you can own a feature from data model to UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relational databases (PostgreSQL preferred) and writing efficient, well-structured queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of REST API design principles and asynchronous patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of writing well-tested code; you care about test coverage and the long-term cost of technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills; you can engage effectively in async and cross-functional team environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive attitude and willingness to learn, adapt, and grow in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to GRC, compliance, audit, or risk management domains — even as an end user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with compliance frameworks such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, NIST CSF, or FedRAMP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building workflow-heavy or state-machine-driven features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with risk registers, control frameworks, or evidence management concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a B2B SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
